---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import MockFrame from "../../components/visuals/MockFrame.astro";
import AiEvalBoard from "../../components/visuals/AiEvalBoard.astro";
import EvalFlowCanvas from "../../components/visuals/EvalFlowCanvas.astro";
import CheckList from "../../components/CheckList.astro";
import RelatedFeatures from "../../components/RelatedFeatures.astro";
---

<Layout title="AI evaluation and optimization — CloudGrid">
  <Section size="lg">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="AI Evaluation"
      accent="violet"
      title="Turn collected telemetry into better AI behavior."
      description="CloudGrid gives AI teams a practical evaluation loop inside the same project where traces, logs, metrics, and dashboards already live: curate datasets, run evaluations, compare outputs, optimize prompts or examples, and promote improvements with evidence."
    />
  </Section>

  <Section tone="recessed">
    <div class="reveal-scale">
      <EvalFlowCanvas />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-text-muted">
      The loop is intentionally simple: evidence becomes dataset rows, evaluations produce results,
      comparisons show what changed, and promotion stays an explicit team decision.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-text">What you can do today</h2>
        <CheckList
          items={[
            "Create schema-backed datasets for classification, extraction, generation, and workflow checks.",
            "Add rows with input, expected output, optional observed output, reason, split, and curation status.",
            "Validate raw JSON input and expected output against the dataset schema before a row becomes ready.",
            "Import trace-derived cases when production evidence reveals a missed classification, extraction, or workflow decision.",
            "Run dataset evaluations against a target using project model aliases and metric defaults.",
            "Inspect per-row expected vs actual output, metric results, trajectory summaries, important steps, and trace links.",
            "Compare baseline and candidate runs to see improvements, regressions, latency tradeoffs, and representative examples.",
            "Use quick-shot optimization to explore candidates, then validate before explicit promotion.",
          ]}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-text">Honest about scope</h2>
        <CheckList
          muted
          items={[
            "The primary v1 workflow is dataset evaluation and optimization. Production measurement is intentionally not the main user flow yet.",
            "Complex agents and workflows can be evaluated through an adapter endpoint instead of rebuilding the whole workflow inside CloudGrid.",
            "Provider API keys belong in project or company provider settings. They are not typed into datasets or evaluation rows.",
            "Evaluation produces metrics, results, and comparisons. Alerting or release gates can consume those values later, but they are not the evaluation itself.",
            "Quick-shot optimization is exploratory. Promotion should use full validation evidence.",
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="mb-8 max-w-3xl reveal">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-text">
        The building blocks are understandable by the whole team.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        A dataset says what good looks like. An evaluation runs a target against that dataset. A
        comparison shows whether the candidate is better or worse. Optimization is the loop that
        proposes changes and proves them against validation data.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-4">
      <div class="card spotlight is-interactive flex h-full flex-col p-6 reveal" data-delay="1">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted">Datasets</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-text">Versioned examples</div>
        <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">Rows contain input, expected output, optional reason, split, curation status, and source evidence.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card spotlight is-interactive flex h-full flex-col p-6 reveal" data-delay="2">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted">Evaluations</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-text">Repeatable runs</div>
        <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">Run a selected target over a dataset split and inspect aggregate and per-row results.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card spotlight is-interactive flex h-full flex-col p-6 reveal" data-delay="3">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted">Comparisons</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-text">Better or worse</div>
        <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">See metric deltas, regressions, improvements, and examples that explain the tradeoff.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card spotlight is-interactive flex h-full flex-col p-6 reveal" data-delay="1">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted">Optimization</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-text">Improve with evidence</div>
        <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">Explore quick-shot candidates, validate them, then explicitly promote the winning target.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="recessed">
    <div class="mb-8 max-w-3xl reveal">
      <div class="chip bg-violet-soft text-[var(--color-violet)]">What a finished evaluation looks like</div>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-text text-balance">
        A scoreboard you can actually hand to your team.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-secondary">
        A run summary is not just one number. CloudGrid keeps the aggregate metrics, row-level
        expected vs actual output, trace links, and short trajectory summaries together so the team
        can decide what to improve next.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <MockFrame title="cloudgrid · /ai-eval · evaluation run">
        <AiEvalBoard />
      </MockFrame>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr]">
      <div class="reveal-x">
        <div class="chip bg-emerald-soft text-[var(--color-emerald)]">Why it belongs with telemetry</div>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-text text-balance">
          Your failed examples already exist in traces.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          Many useful evaluation rows start as production evidence: a wrong category, a missing JSON
          field, a tool call that went down the wrong path, or a workflow that took too many steps.
          CloudGrid keeps the source trace link next to the dataset row and the evaluation result,
          so debugging and optimization stay connected.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-3 reveal">
        {[
          ["Classify", "Capture customer messages and expected categories, then measure prompt changes against validation and test splits."],
          ["Extract", "Validate raw JSON outputs against a dataset schema and see exactly which rows failed."],
          ["Workflow", "Keep bounded trajectory summaries and important steps so complex agent runs can be reviewed without opening every span."],
          ["Optimize", "Let candidates compete against the same dataset, then promote only after validation evidence is visible."],
        ].map(([title, body]) => (
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-border-subtle bg-surface p-4">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-text">{title}</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="recessed">
    <RelatedFeatures
      items={[
        { label: "Traces", href: "/features/traces", desc: "Where trace-derived dataset cases and run evidence stay linkable." },
        { label: "Handbook", href: "/handbook/evaluations", desc: "How to create datasets, run evaluations, and optimize targets." },
        { label: "Compare vs", href: "/enterprise/compare", desc: "CloudGrid vs Langfuse, Arize, Braintrust, and APM tools." },
      ]}
    />
  </Section>
</Layout>
